          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %em
                  simplicial
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulation"} triangulation
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr(X)
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %mi Tr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo |
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi homeo
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\vert Tr(X)\right\vert \xrightarrow{homeo} X
                from its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                a
                %em combinatorial triangulation
                is a simplicial triangulation such that for each simplex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                the
                %em link
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                of all simplices
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                that intersect
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                such that both
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                are faces of a simplex) is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
                to a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
          %p
            A
            %em triangulation conjecture
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjectures
            and
            %em triangulation theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proves
            that a given kind of triangulation exists for a given kind of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %em not
            generally exists for a given class of manifolds.
          %h2#statements Statements
          %h3#existence_of_triangulations Existence of triangulations
          %p
            It is easy to show that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/piecewise-linear+manifold"} piecewise-linear manifold
            admits a combinatorial triangulation, so that combinatorial triangulability is often understood to mean existence of a piecewise-linear structure.
          %p A compatible piecewise-linear structure, hence a combinatorial triangulation, hence a simplicial triangulation, does exist for
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#Cairns35"}> Cairns 1935
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#Whitehead40"} Whitehead 1940
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                2, hence every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#Rado25"}> Rado 1924
                )
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                3, hence every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-manifold"} 3-manifold
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#Moise52"}> Moise 1952
                )
          %h3#nonexistence_of_triangulations Non-existence of triangulations
          %p
            In each dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq
            4 there exist
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            %em not
            admitting a combinatorial triangulation (
            %a{:href => "#KirbySiebenmann69"}> Kirby &amp; Siebenmann 1969
            ).
          %p
            In each dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq
            5 there exist
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            %em not
            even admitting a simplicial triangulation (
            %a{:href => "#Manolescu16"}> Manolescu 2016
            )
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(X) \leq 3
            triangulations still exist in general, but for every dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 4
            there exist topological manifolds which do not admit a triangulation. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(X) \geq 5
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ;
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(X) \in H^4(X; \mathbb{Z}/2)
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group+of+order+2"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            admits a triangulation if and only if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(X) = 0
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+triangulation+theorem"} equivariant triangulation theorem
          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#triangulation_theorems_for_manifolds Triangulation theorems for manifolds
            %p
              On
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulation+conjectures"} triangulation conjectures
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulation+theorems"} triangulation theorems
              on existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulations"} triangulations
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ciprian+Manolescu"}> Ciprian Manolescu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Triangulations of manifolds
                %strong 2
                2 (2014) (
                %a{:href => "https://web.stanford.edu/~cm5/tm.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Manolescu_TriangulationsOfManifolds.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/ICCM.2014.v2.n2.a2"} doi:10.4310/ICCM.2014.v2.n2.a2
            %p
              The question of triangulability of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              was first raised in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Poincar%C3%A9"}> Henri Poincaré
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Complément à l’analysis situs
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF03024461"} doi:10.1007/BF03024461
            %p
              and for general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
              in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hellmuth+Kneser"}> Hellmuth Kneser
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Die Topologie der Mannigfaltigkeiten
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/145701"} eudml:145701
            %p
              Proof that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              admits a combinatorial triangulation:
            %ul
              %li#Rado25
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tibor+Rad%C3%B3"}> Tibor Radó
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Über den Begriff der Riemannschen Fläche
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/rado.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://acta.bibl.u-szeged.hu/13312/1/math_002_101-121.pdf"} pdf
                %p
                  Proof that every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                  admits a combinatorial triangulation:
            %p
              Proof that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              admits a combinatorial triangulation is due to
            %ul
              %li#Cairns35
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stewart+S.+Cairns"}> Stewart S. Cairns
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Triangulation of the manifold of class one
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-american-mathematical-society-new-series/volume-41/issue-8/Triangulation-of-the-manifold-of-class-one/bams/1183498332.full"} euclid:1183498332
              %li#Whitehead40
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+H.+C.+Whitehead"}> J. H. C. Whitehead
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      On
                      = succeed "-complexes" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1968861"} doi:10.2307/1968861
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1968861"} jstor:1968861
            %p with further accounts in:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hassler+Whitney"}> Hassler Whitney
                  , Section IV.B of:
                  %em Geometric Integration Theory
                  (1957), Princeton Legacy Library (2016) (
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/9781400877577"}> doi:10.1515/9781400877577
                  )
              %li#Cairns61
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stewart+S.+Cairns"}> Stewart S. Cairns
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A simple triangulation method for smooth manifolds
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9904-1961-10631-9"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9904-1961-10631-9
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    (but see
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/177199/381"} MO:a/177199
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                  ,
                  %em Existence of Triangulations
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/937notes/937Lecture4.pdf"}> pdf
                  ), Lecture 4 in:
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/937.html"} Topics in Geometric Topology
            %p A detailed exposition is available in Chapter II (see Thm. 10.6) of
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+R.+Munkres"}> James R. Munkres
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elementary Differential Topology
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1515/9781400882656"} doi:10.1515/9781400882656
            %p
              Generalization to existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+triangulation"} equivariant triangulation
              for smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifolds"} G-manifolds
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+triangulation+theorem"}> equivariant triangulation theorem
              ):
            %ul
              %li#Illman72
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S%C3%B6ren+Illman"}> Sören Illman
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Equivariant algebraic topology
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Illman_EquivariantAlgebraicTopology1972.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li#Illman78
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S%C3%B6ren+Illman"}> Sören Illman
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Smooth equivariant triangulations of
                      = succeed "-manifolds" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi G
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi G
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                      a finite group
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01405351"} doi:10.1007/BF01405351
              %li#Illman83
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S%C3%B6ren+Illman"}> Sören Illman
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Equivariant Triangulation Theorem for Actions of Compact Lie Groups
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/163720"} dml:163720
            %p
              Proof that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-manifold"} 3-manifold
              admits the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and hence of a combinatorial triangulation:
            %ul
              %li#Moise52
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+E.+Moise"}> Edwin E. Moise
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Affine Structures in 3-Manifolds: V. The Triangulation Theorem and Hauptvermutung
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1969769"} doi:10.2307/1969769
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1969769"} jstor:1969769
            %p
              Proof that in every dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim \geq 4
              there exist topological manifolds without combinatorial triangulation:
            %ul
              %li#KirbySiebenmann69
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robion+C.+Kirby"}> Robion C. Kirby
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+C.+Siebenmann"} Laurent C. Siebenmann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the triangulation of manifolds and the Hauptvermutung
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-american-mathematical-society/volume-75/issue-4/On-the-triangulation-of-manifolds-and-the-Hauptvermutung/bams/1183530633.full"} euclid:1183530633
            %p
              Proof that in every dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim \geq 5
              there exist topological manifolds without simplicial triangulation:
            %ul
              %li#Manolescu16
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ciprian+Manolescu"}> Ciprian Manolescu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Pin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pin(2)
                    \-equivariant Seiberg-Witten Floer homology and the Triangulation Conjecture
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.2354"} arXiv:1303.2354
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/jams829"} doi:10.1090/jams829
